# Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) for `wrangler dev`.
#
# There is deliberately no Supabase service-role key here, and there should
# never be one. The server verifies tokens with the project's *public* JWKS, so
# it needs no credential that could be used to mint an identity or read a table.
# If a future feature seems to need the service key, that is the moment to ask
# whether the client should be doing it against Supabase's own row-level
# security instead.

# Your Supabase project URL. Leave empty to run the server with no identity
# provider — /health will say `identityConfigured: false` and sockets will be
# refused, which is the honest behaviour rather than a permissive one.
SUPABASE_URL=""

# Guards POST /match/:id/init until the matchmaker (§9) exists to own it.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32
ADMIN_TOKEN=""
